# ComposeIO / ComposeUX — platform domain profile [PROFILE:PROFILE-COMPOSEIO]

> The `.lts` successor to `corpora/platform-specs/99-composeio-profile.yaml`, authored to close
> [FIX-LTS-PROFILE-DRIFTED-FROM-CORPUS]. The yaml declared 38 prefixes in a punctuation form V1
> cannot match (`BP-EXT-`, `CXC-HALD-`) while every prefix the corpus actually mints went
> unregistered. Every registration below was DERIVED by scanning `corpora/**/*.lts` and carries its
> observed count in an `evidence` property, so the drift is re-checkable rather than re-assertable.
>
> ⛔ BOOTSTRAPPING INVARIANT. This document is parsed with CORE notation only — it cannot use the
> vocabulary it registers, or the profile would be needed in order to parse the profile
> (`factlattice/profile.py::_assert_core_only_parse`). There is therefore NO `## Relationships`
> section here, no namespaced edge type, and no relationship-bearing property. Every construct is a
> plain heading node with plain `- key: value` properties.

---

## [PROFILE-DOMAIN] Domain identity

- domain-id: plt.cio
- domain-name: ComposePlatform — ComposeIO bus + ComposeUX composer
- domain-version: 2.0
- conventions-source: corpora/platform-specs/99-composeio-profile.yaml (the yaml predecessor this document supersedes) + 99-composeio-conventions.smd (the prose narrative of record)
- namespaces: plt.cio, plt.cux
- evidence: `domain: plt.cux` in 62 corpus files and `domain: plt.cio` in 2; 31 cross-corpus references authored as `[plt.cio:SPEC:*]` (24) and `[plt.cux:SPEC:*]` (7)

