## Registered node-id prefixes

> V1 compares a node's `type_prefix` — the id text BEFORE THE FIRST HYPHEN — against this set, with
> trailing hyphens normalized off both sides. `CXC-IC-LAUNCH` therefore has type_prefix `CXC`, and a
> registration of `CXC-IC-` could never match it. That is the precise shape of the drift being
> closed: register the FIRST SEGMENT, not the sub-family.

### [PREFIX-CXC] ComposeUX / ComposeIO Composer spec nodes

- registers-prefix: CXC-
- document: corpora/platform-specs (the whole spec corpus)
- definition: The platform's primary node family; sub-families (CXC-R-, CXC-IC-, CXC-HAL-, CXC-TERM-, CXC-PRIM-, ...) all resolve to this one type prefix
- evidence: 641 heading nodes across 49 files, plus 44 document roots of the form [SPEC:CXC-*]

