## Registered node-id prefixes — MIGRATED FROM THE YAML PREDECESSOR

> Every registration in this section was carried over from `99-composeio-profile.yaml` when that file
> was retired. The yaml declared 39 prefixes; 21 of them normalize onto first segments this profile
> already registers (`CXC-`, `CIO-`, `CAP-`, `DX-`, `DP-`) and are recorded as sub-families in those
> nodes' definitions rather than as separate registrations that could never match — see
> [GUIDANCE-PREFIX-FIRST-SEGMENT]. The 18 below are the yaml's genuinely distinct FIRST SEGMENTS.
>
> ⚠ Two of them — `DASH-` and `REN-` — were carrying 71 live `unregistered_prefix` findings against
> this corpus for as long as the two profiles were separate: the yaml declared them and the yaml was
> only ever discovered for `corpora/platform-specs`, while this profile, which did not, was the one
> the intelligence-console root discovered. That is the measured cost of two vocabularies.
>
> The other 16 address the ComposeIO core spec corpus (`spec/`), which no corpus-config root
> currently includes. They are declared-but-unused today and cost nothing: V1 only ever checks
> USED-against-DECLARED, so an unused registration produces no finding. They are carried anyway
> because dropping a registration nobody is currently exercising is precisely how vocabulary is
> silently lost.

