## Registered document tags

> Only the DOMAIN half belongs here. V2 unions this set with SPEC §1.7's core tags, so SPEC (48
> documents), SYSTEM (1) and PROJECT (1) are already valid and are deliberately NOT re-declared —
> re-declaring core vocabulary is how a profile starts to look like a definition of the format.

### [DOCTAG-LEDGER] Append-only ledger

- document-tag: LEDGER
- definition: A ledger of records rather than a specification — the deliverable ledger, the strategy ledger, and the principles ledger
- evidence: 3 documents (deliverable-ledger.lts, strategies.lts, principles.lts)

### [DOCTAG-REGISTRY] Registry

- document-tag: REGISTRY
- definition: A registry of named entities the platform addresses by id
- evidence: 1 document (projects.lts)

### [DOCTAG-PROFILE] Domain profile

- document-tag: PROFILE
- definition: A `.lts` domain profile, per [PROFILE-SELFHOST] — a profile is a document parsed by the parser it configures
- evidence: 1 document (this file)

### [DOCTAG-AMEND] Amendment to an existing spec

- document-tag: AMEND
- definition: An amendment to an existing specification; uses the `amends:` frontmatter key. MIGRATED from the yaml predecessor, which declared SPEC, SYSTEM and AMEND — SPEC and SYSTEM are SPEC §1.7 CORE tags (`CORE_DOCUMENT_TAGS` in `factlattice_engine/lint/profile_rules.py`) that V2 unions in already, so re-declaring them would only restate the format; AMEND is genuinely domain vocabulary and would have been lost with the yaml
- evidence: no document currently DECLARES itself `[AMEND:*]` in the registered corpora, but 4 qualified cross-references author the doctype (`[AMEND:BP-CAPTURE-REPLAY]`, `[AMEND:CS-APP]` in 10-composer-runtime-dashboard.lts) against the un-migrated ComposeIO core spec corpus

